course: dictionary
lesson: 10105
title: Thinly: thin layers, few people, hidden feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Thinly is an adverb. It tells you how something is spread, cut or shown. Its meaning changes with the words around it, so read the clues before you choose a meaning.
explain: Meaning one is about thickness: «Spread the butter thinly» means use only a small amount, in a thin layer. Meaning two is about few things spread over a large space: «Stars are spread out very thinly, with huge empty spaces between them.» Meaning three is about hiding something badly: «a thinly disguised trick» is easy to see through.
explain: Ask yourself what is thin. If it is a layer or a slice, think about thickness. If the sentence talks about people, animals or space, think few and far apart. If it talks about a trick or a feeling, think easy to see through. Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Thinly means in a thin layer or in thin pieces: «slice thinly».
fact: Thinly also means with few people or things spread over a large area: «thinly populated».
fact: Thinly can mean only slightly, so that it is easy to see through: «a thinly disguised trick».
fact: In geography, «thinly populated» places, such as the Australian outback, have only a few people for each big area of land.
fact: Thinly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done or spread.
exercise: «Spread the butter thinly on the bread.» What does thinly mean here? | In a straight line | *In a thin layer | With a big pile of butter | Very quickly and loudly
exercise: «Stars are spread out very thinly, with huge empty spaces between them.» What does thinly mean here? | *With few stars over a large space | Very brightly | Close together in a crowd | In thin, pale colours
exercise: «a thinly disguised trick» What does thinly tell you about the trick? | It is a long trick | *It is only slightly hidden, so it is easy to see through | It is made of thin paper | It is hidden very well
test: «Ella says the cook must slice the apple thinly.» What action is that? | Put it in a box | *Cut it into thin slices | Eat it whole | Cook it for hours
test: «Thinly populated» places have what? | *Few people spread over a large area | Very many people | Lots of water | Tall buildings
exam: «each tiger needs a big area of its own because its prey is spread out thinly» Why does each tiger need a big area? | Tigers are very heavy and slow | *Its prey is spread out, with few animals over a large space | Tigers need a lot of sunlight | Tigers like to play in big fields
